BSX3 -- WHY NO KINETIC FUNCTION REPAIRS THE KHRONON-DUST AETHER, AND THE PHANTOM'S MASS BUDGET.
(1) For ANY K(Q), the static mass term a galaxy feels and the late cosmological Jeans scale of the khronon are the
same scale: mu_eff^2 = k_J,phys^2 (1 + c_ad^2), exactly.  KiDS's external-field bound needs a short Jeans length,
MOND-like lensing to ~1 Mpc needs a long mass-term range; the identity makes them one number, so the BSX1 pincer
holds for every K.  (2) BSX2's cubic 'repair' (PAPER33 v1) is withdrawn: at the parameters that passed cosmology its
K-sector density in a galaxy exceeds the MOND phantom by ~1e7 and its mass-term range is a few kpc.  (3) The mass-
budget gate the phantom-as-conserved-fluid picture owes: where does the deep-MOND phantom of a KiDS lens exhaust
the dark fluid it can have assembled?

(1) THE IDENTITY (symbolic, general K).  BS24's khronon on FRW: 8 pi G rho = Q K_Q - K, 8 pi G P = K (their eqs. 44,
54, 57), so c_ad^2 = dP/drho = K_Q/(Q K_QQ) and the Jeans wavenumber of their eq. 71 is
    k_J,phys^2 = 4 pi G rho (1 + w)/c_ad^2 = (1/2) Q^2 K_QQ .
In a static region Q = Q_bar (1 - Xi/c^2) (their eq. 18a with the cosmic Q_bar), and the K part of the 00 equation,
-(c^2/2) delta(Q K_Q), linearises to mu_eff^2 Xi with
    mu_eff^2 = (1/2) Q (K_Q + Q K_QQ)  =>  mu_eff^2 / k_J,phys^2 = 1 + K_Q/(Q K_QQ) = 1 + c_ad^2 .
BS24's quadratic K reproduces their eq. 25 (mu^2 Xi) and their k_J = a mu.  The identity is exact.

(2) THE CUBIC REPAIR AT ITS OWN PARAMETERS.  K = (2M^2/3)(Q-1)^3 at the M^2 that BSX2 found passing cosmology (late
Jeans length 0.3-3 kpc): the linear mass-term range 1/mu_eff equals that Jeans length, so r_C = (r_M/mu_eff^2)^(1/3)
is a few kpc; and the nonlinear K density M^2 Xi^2/(4 pi G c^2) at galactic potentials dwarfs the MOND phantom.
BSX2's X1 (the cubic term is "1PN") was a formal c -> infinity limit at fixed M^2 and does not hold at M^2 ~ 1e17
Mpc^-2.

(3) THE MASS BUDGET.  A conserved phantom (BSK1 M2) must be assembled from dark fluid that fell in.  The deep-MOND
phantom inside r is M_ph(<r) = (r/r_M - 1) M_b.  Two budgets for a lens of baryonic mass M_b:
  (a) generous: the LCDM halo mass M_200 of its stellar mass (Moster, Naab & White 2013 SHMR at z = 0.25), i.e. the
      dark fluid falls in as CDM does; (b) tight: the galaxy's own cosmic share (Omega_dm/Omega_b) M_b.
  The budget radius is where M_ph(<r) reaches the budget.  KiDS-1000 isolated lenses (Brouwer+2021) are clean to
  R = 0.3 Mpc and measured to 3 Mpc.

==============================================================================================================
I1  THE IDENTITY: mu_eff^2 = k_J,phys^2 (1 + c_ad^2) for ANY K(Q)
==============================================================================================================
    c_ad^2 = Derivative(K(Q), Q)/(Q*Derivative(K(Q), (Q, 2)));   k_J,phys^2 = Q**2*Derivative(K(Q), (Q, 2))/2
    static mass term mu_eff^2 = Qbar*(Qbar*Derivative(K(Qbar), (Qbar, 2)) + Derivative(K(Qbar), Qbar))/2
    mu_eff^2 / k_J^2 = 1 + Derivative(K(Qbar), Qbar)/(Qbar*Derivative(K(Qbar), (Qbar, 2)))
    quadratic K (BS24): mu_eff^2 -> mu2,  k_J^2 -> mu2   (their eq. 25's mu^2 and k_J = a mu)
    cubic K:           mu_eff^2 = M2*q*(q + 1)*(3*q + 2),  k_J^2 = 2*M2*q*(q + 1)**2
  [PASS] I1 for any K(Q): the static mass term a galaxy feels equals the late Jeans scale of the khronon, mu_eff^2 = k_J,phys^2 (1 + c_ad^2) exactly (checked on BS24's quadratic K and on the cubic K)
         measured: mu_eff^2/k_J^2 = 1 + Derivative(K(Qbar), Qbar)/(Qbar*Derivative(K(Qbar), (Qbar, 2))); quadratic -> (mu^2, mu^2); cubic ratio -> 1 as q -> 0
         reading:  the same second derivative K_QQ at the cosmic background sets both; no choice of K separates them

==============================================================================================================
I2  BSX2's CUBIC 'REPAIR' AT ITS OWN PASSING PARAMETERS: MOND ends at a few kpc; the K density dwarfs the phantom
==============================================================================================================
    lambda_J,0 =  0.3 kpc: q0 = 3.60e-15;  1/mu_eff = 0.3 kpc;  r_C(MW) = 0.947 kpc;  K density / MOND phantom at 10/30/100 kpc = 1.5e+12 / 8.6e+12 / 5.1e+13
    lambda_J,0 =    1 kpc: q0 = 4.01e-14;  1/mu_eff = 1 kpc;  r_C(MW) = 2.11 kpc;  K density / MOND phantom at 10/30/100 kpc = 1.2e+10 / 6.9e+10 / 4.1e+11
    lambda_J,0 =    3 kpc: q0 = 3.60e-13;  1/mu_eff = 3 kpc;  r_C(MW) = 4.4 kpc;  K density / MOND phantom at 10/30/100 kpc = 1.5e+08 / 8.6e+08 / 5.1e+09
  [PASS] I2 at every late Jeans length that BSX2 found passing cosmology (0.3-3 kpc), the cubic khronon's galactic mass-term range is that Jeans length, MOND ends inside ~10 kpc, and its K density at 10 kpc exceeds the MOND phantom by >= 1e6: BSX2's repair (PAPER33 v1) is withdrawn
         measured: max r_C(MW) = 4.4 kpc; min K/phantom density at 10 kpc = 1.47e+08
         reading:  BSX2 X1's 'the cubic term is 1PN' is a c -> infinity limit at fixed M^2; the passing M^2 (~1e15-1e17 Mpc^-2) is not O(c^0), so the term is not negligible -- a formal PN count must be evaluated at the parameters used

==============================================================================================================
I3  THE PINCER FOR EVERY K: KiDS's field bound needs k_J large, MOND to ~1 Mpc needs mu_eff small
==============================================================================================================
    BSX1 (their filter k^2/(k^2 + k_J^2), CDM-like khronon spectrum on large scales): the KiDS external-field bound
    needs 1/k_J,phys <~ 0.22 Mpc at z = 0.25.  BS24's eq. 38: r_C = (r_M/mu_eff^2)^(1/3) >= 1 Mpc for a Milky-Way
    lens needs 1/mu_eff >= (1 Mpc^3/r_M)^(1/2).  With mu_eff = k_J (1 + c_ad^2)^(1/2), c_ad^2 << 1 today:
    MOND to 1 Mpc: 1/mu_eff >= 10.3 Mpc;  KiDS field bound: 1/k_J <= 0.223 Mpc  -> gap x46
  [PASS] I3 (the pincer for every K) the scale KiDS's field bound needs (<= 0.22 Mpc) and the scale MOND-like lensing to 1 Mpc needs (>= ~10 Mpc) differ by a factor ~40 and are, by I1, the same scale
         measured: 1/mu_eff >= 10.3 Mpc vs 1/k_J <= 0.223 Mpc
         reading:  r_C is BS24's order-of-magnitude eq. 38 and the field bound is linear theory; the factor ~40 gap is what makes the statement robust to those approximations

==============================================================================================================
B  THE MASS BUDGET: where the deep-MOND phantom of a KiDS lens exhausts the dark fluid it can have assembled
==============================================================================================================
    log M* 10.0: M_b = 1.40e+10, M_200 (Moster+13, z = 0.25) = 4.17e+11 Msun, r_M = 4.6 kpc;  budget radius: generous 0.14 Mpc, tight 29 kpc (canonical)
    log M* 10.5: M_b = 4.42e+10, M_200 (Moster+13, z = 0.25) = 1.01e+12 Msun, r_M = 8.1 kpc;  budget radius: generous 0.19 Mpc, tight 52 kpc (canonical)
    log M* 10.7: M_b = 7.00e+10, M_200 (Moster+13, z = 0.25) = 1.90e+12 Msun, r_M = 10.2 kpc;  budget radius: generous 0.29 Mpc, tight 65 kpc (canonical)
    log M* 10.9: M_b = 1.12e+11, M_200 (Moster+13, z = 0.25) = 5.66e+12 Msun, r_M = 12.9 kpc;  budget radius: generous 0.67 Mpc, tight 82 kpc (canonical)
  [PASS] B1 (measurement) the budget radius with CDM-like accretion (M_200 from Moster+13) against the KiDS-1000 clean isolated-lens radius 0.3 Mpc, per stellar-mass bin and footing
         measured: generous budget radius 0.13-0.67 Mpc; bins/footings running out inside 0.3 Mpc: 6/8
         reading:  a conserved phantom can only be as large as the dark fluid the galaxy accreted; the deep-MOND phantom grows linearly with radius (M_ph = (r/r_M - 1) M_b), a LCDM halo does not
  [PASS] B2 (measurement) the same with only the galaxy's own cosmic share (Omega_dm/Omega_b) M_b
         measured: tight budget radius <= 82 kpc
         reading:  the swarm lane BSK3's KiDS failure (+91 inside 0.3 Mpc) corresponds to a budget of this kind; BSK3 itself is not reproduced here

==============================================================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================================================
  (1) For any kinetic function K(Q), the static mass term a galaxy feels and the khronon's late Jeans scale are one
  scale, mu_eff^2 = k_J^2 (1 + c_ad^2) (I1).  KiDS's external-field bound needs that scale short (<= 0.22 Mpc) and
  MOND-like lensing to ~1 Mpc needs it long (>= ~10 Mpc): the khronon-as-dark-fluid aether of Blanchet &
  Skordis is closed by KiDS for every K, not only for their benchmarks (I3 with BSX1).
  (2) PAPER33 v1's cubic repair is withdrawn: at its passing parameters MOND ends inside ~4 kpc and the
  K density dwarfs the phantom by >= 1e6 (I2).  The one-scale identity a0 = kappa c sqrt(G rho_Lambda) of v1's X3 is
  algebra and stands.
  (3) The budget: with CDM-like accretion the conserved phantom of a KiDS lens runs out at 0.13-0.67 Mpc
  (6 of 8 bin/footing cases inside the 0.3 Mpc clean radius); with only the galaxy's own cosmic
  share it runs out by 82 kpc.  A conserved phantom reproduces KiDS's MOND-like lensing only if galaxies
  accrete more dark fluid than LCDM halos hold at those radii -- a question for nonlinear growth in the theory.
  Design lesson: the MOND function must not read the acceleration of the cosmological dark fluid.

